<title>SWITZERLAND: Roche seeks Corange takeover approvals.</title>
<headline>Roche seeks Corange takeover approvals.</headline>
<dateline>BASLE, Switzerland 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Roche Holding AG said it applied for U.S. Federal Trade Commission and European Commission approvals of its takeover of Corange Ltd.</p>
<p>Roche announced plans in May to purchase Bermuda-based Corange as part of a complex $11 billion deal to acquire the diagnostics and pharmaceuticals company Boehringer Mannheim Group.</p>
<p>Corange is the sole owner of Boehringer Mannheim. It also holds an 84.2 percent stake in DePuy Inc, a maker of orthopaedic products.</p>
<p>Roche said in a statement today that in the meantime both groups will continue to exchange relevant information and begin planning the future integration so that the first concrete proposals can be worked out by September.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
